### C. Comparison


In our algorithms, we need to perform addition mod N of a c-number a and a q-number b.
An important step in modular addition is comparison—we must find out whether a+ b ≥ N.
Thus, our next task is to devise a unitary operation that compares a c-number and a qnumber. This operation should, say, flip a target bit if the c-number is greater than the
q-number, and leave the target bit alone otherwise.
A conceptually simple way to compare a K-bit c-number a and a K-bit q-number b is
to devise an adder that computes the sum of the c-number 2K − 1 − a and the q-number
