FIG. 5. The multiplexed full adder M U XF A′′ (a0 , a1 ) (shown here for a0 = 0, a1 = 1) is a
modification of M U XF A that uses an extra bit of scratch space. The first gate stores L ∧ ℓ in
the extra scratch qubit, and subsequent gates use this scratch bit as a control bit. The last gate
clears the scratch bit. The advantage of M U XF A′′ is that the longest control string required by
any gate is shorter by one bit than the longest control string required in M U XF A.

